{"status":"read","documents":[{"ref":"Df7c9f19677a073980f80","sha256":"f7c9f19677a073980f80259596f33542d98ff6ebb164b086c5c608acbbca72bc","pointer":"/result","offset":0,"text":"{"status":"read","documents":[{"ref":"D52372128b94c880c9283","sha256":"52372128b94c880c92833073c337931b55206c96516bdf02e16cdf13c1c37600","pointer":"/sources","offset":21400,"text":"/39475\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.5772/39475\",\"text\":\"Extracting Individual Properties from Global Behaviour: First-order Reversal Curve Method Applied to Magnetic Nanowire Arrays\",\"access\":\"indexed_abstract_only\",\"date_evidence\":\"OpenAlex publication_date\",\"id\":\"Ka21bf6100e3a12cc\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-10T08:04:36.334907+00:00\",\"query\":\"nonreciprocal Preisach model\"},{\"title\":\"Passive and active field theories for disease spreading\",\"date\":\"2024-05-15\",\"publication_dates\":[\"2024-05-15\"],\"doi\":\"https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8121/ad4c31\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8121/ad4c31\",\"text\":\"Abstract The worldwide COVID-19 pandemic has led to a significant growth of interest in the development of mathematical models that allow to describe effects such as social distancing measures, the development of vaccines, and mutations. Several of these models are based on concepts from soft matter theory. Considerably less well investigated is the reverse direction, i.e. how results from epidemiological research can be of interest for the physics of colloids and polymers. In this work, we consider the susceptible-infected-recovered (SIR)-dynamical density functional theory (DDFT) model, a combination of the SIR model from epidemiology with DDFT from nonequilibrium soft matter physics, which allows for an explicit modeling of social distancing. We extend the SIR-DDFT model both from an epidemiological perspective by incorporating vaccines, asymptomaticity, reinfections, and mutations, and from a soft matter perspective by incorporating noise and self-propulsion and by deriving a phase field crystal (PFC) model that allows for a simplified description. On this basis, we investigate via computer simulations how epidemiological models are affected by the presence of non-reciprocal interactions. This is done in a numerical study of a zombie outbreak.\",\"access\":\"indexed_abstract_only\",\"date_evidence\":\"OpenAlex publication_date\",\"id\":\"K76f48790bf6b54ab\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-10T08:04:36.352388+00:00\",\"query\":\"nonreciprocal Preisach model\"}]","next_offset":null,"total_characters":23462,"raw_original":false},{"ref":"Dc2f530d8695d2a174da1","sha256":"c2f530d8695d2a174da1608db6116d54df0d25151e710e44653b489d0deed11d","pointer":"/hypothesis_updates","offset":0,"text":"[{\"assumption\":\"本装置每个转子的态不是双阱势的 ±1，而是「被单侧止挡支撑的受限平衡」：释放条件是合力矩为零（驱动与耦合弹簧合力过枢轴，即共线），与弹簧刚度无关；回路半宽 h 是止挡角跨度的几何换算，不是势垒高度；此外存在第三个可容许态（离位浮动），其稳定性由释放处合成弹簧力是拉伸还是压缩（R 与静长 ℓ0 的比较）决定。\",\"base_version\":0,\"conceptual_move\":\"把「双稳」的来源从能量景观换成运动学约束（止挡）＋力过枢轴；于是「停用/新建软点」不必经过宽度改变，而「易切换 vs 保住次序」也不必落在同一条能量轴上。\",\"depends_on\":[],\"implications\":[\"条件性：事件次序只由释放面排列决定，因而与 k_d、k_c 无关；只改刚度时次序不变，但 b、1−w 与释放时释放的能量会变。\",\"条件性：浮动会让转子在一整段驱动里沉默但不「卡住」；判别标志是力-γ 曲线的有限斜率支，以及该类沉默结束时的力跳变小于止挡释放。\",\"条件性：若释放处 R<ℓ0（压缩），内点不稳定，转子必须吸附到某一止挡，因此该转子不可能浮动；同一几何可通过换静长在「吸附式双稳」与「连续可逆」之间切换。\"],\"influenced_by\":[{\"key\":\"threshold_coordinate_factorization\",\"owner\":\"theory_scientist\",\"version\":2},{\"key\":\"clamp_admissibility_limits\",\"owner\":\"theory_scientist\",\"version\":1}],\"key\":\"unilateral_stop_state\",\"motivation\":\"ell=0 的四个阈值被「共线阈值」零参数复现到 ≤0.3 cm；pair_A 两转子在释放处的 R−ℓ0 符号相反（条件性算例 +1.52 vs −0.92 cm），说明「同一几何」的两个转子可以是不同力学类型；network_C 有两处「该翻未翻」需要一个非 ±1 的态来解释。\",\"open_questions\":[\"pair_A 两转子位于静长两侧这一算例是否可信（依赖 L_cm=6.3 与 y=9.4 的读法，而阈值公式与 L 无关，故未被检验）？\",\"network_C 的止挡角与静长未记录，无法判断哪个转子可能浮动？\",\"浮动与「状态依赖阈值」在只有事件表时是否永远不可区分？\"],\"reason\":\"它把三条互不相干的观察（阈值共线、两转子类型差异、缺失事件）放到一个力学前提上，并给出可判别的观测量；但核心数值算例未被数据检验，故保留 developing。\",\"status\":\"developing\"},{\"assumption\":\"peer 的三个坐标（中心漂移、共用收缩 w(L)、邻居偏置 b）不是三个独立机制，而是同一个耦合力矩函数 T_c(θ, σ_邻) 在「两个止挡 × 两个邻态」2×2 网格上的对称/反对称分解：b 是邻态方向的差、1−w 是止挡方向的差，两者都由「耦合力 × 力臂 / 驱动的 γ 灵敏度」给出，故同标度（∝ ell²）且同随 k_c/k_d 变化。\",\"base_version\":0,\"conce","next_offset":4000,"total_characters":6411,"raw_original":true},{"ref":"D9a9043b36c2a54d4a1bf","sha256":"9a9043b36c2a54d4a1bfcf1a05b3c4ba29b7a38e66c46fac16e20424a1c23ca0","pointer":"","offset":0,"text":"{
